# legacy static site is kept on disk for reference and as the image-pipeline
# source, but its raw media (372MB+ of uncompressed camera photos/video) does
# not belong in git history — the client code/markup is still tracked.
_legacy-static-site/client/images/
_legacy-static-site/client/videos/
# server/ has its own nested git repo (a different remote); tracking it here
# would create an embedded-repo gitlink instead of real files. It's kept on
# disk, untracked, purely for reference during the Phase B rebuild.
_legacy-static-site/server/
